From 9f6a30fa63b492179582fc87cb8d1a9f34491437 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 06:55:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] escha vulkan: column ladder C2/C4/C8/C16, and the generator
 table measured and REFUTED

THE LADDER. One weight decode costs ~6 operations and feeds ONE multiply-add per column, so the
kernel does C multiply-adds per decode. Only two rungs existed, C=1 and C=8, which wasted half the
lanes at 4 columns and paid two decode passes at 16. The ladder adds C=2/4/16 and picks the smallest
rung that covers ncols, the widest once ncols passes it. GGML_VK_ESCHA_MAX_COLS caps it for A/B.

Effect on the speculative curve, which was violently non-monotonic before (decode 5.53 at n_max=3,
2.91 at 7, 10.03 at 9 - the dips landing exactly where rung selection flipped). With the ladder the
curve flattens and lifts: every depth from 7 up sits near 10.3-10.5 against plain 3.92.

THE TABLE, REFUTED. escha_F is a pure function of a 16-bit codeword, so all 65,536 values fit in
128 KiB. The estate had closed this by reasoning; an unverified refusal is not evidence, so it was
built and measured:
    arithmetic generator   pp512 16.78   tg32 3.92
    65,536-entry table     pp512 16.62   tg32 0.80
4.9x slower on decode. The reasoning was right. Kept behind GGML_VK_ESCHA_LUT with the numbers.

A REGRESSION I CAUSED AND FIXED. The table was first wired by declaring binding 4 in every escha
variant so one layout could serve both arms, on the assumption an unused binding is free. It is not:
binding a fifth buffer on all 13,200 decode dispatches cost 4.8x (3.91 -> 0.81), and it was caught
only because a saved pre-ladder binary was re-run on the same box minutes later. The table now binds
on the table arm alone.

The table is also built on FIRST USE, not at device init: ggml_vk_buffer_write needs queues and a
command pool that do not exist while pipelines are still being created, and doing it there crashed
every binary with an access violation the moment the device was enumerated.

Correctness: test-backend-ops -o ESCHA_MM, 20 cases, 22 OK, 0 FAIL, on BOTH generator arms. New
cases cover every rung full and ragged (ncols 3/5/16/17) plus C16 at model depth, because a case
only ever proves the rung its ncols selects.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
